      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Acute experiments on unconscious rats have demonstrated that fructose-1,6-diphosphate, phosphoenolpyruvate and malate of sodium produced a marked antiarrhythmic activity in acute occlusive and reperfusion arrhythmias, prevented the development of ventricular fibrillation and tachycardias, considerably reduced the duration of arrhythmia paroxysms, but they were ineffective in ventricular extrasystole."},
